        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0539" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/6–1146</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Legal Adviser</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-11">June 11, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In conference with Mr. Barnett of the FEC staff
                    today, following up the conference with General McCoy, I advised that there was
                    no legal objection to the attached proposal but urged, as a matter of policy,
                    that subparagraph (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) should be deferred so as to
                    maintain the position of the United States that such matters should be settled
                    under correct principles. If the Reparations Commission is promptly set up and
                    determines that Russia is entitled to a certain amount, and if under (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) of the draft the inventory is filed and shows
                    that the total commingled amount which Russia has is not more than she is
                    entitled to, there would never be an occasion for a definition of war booty. The
                    decision could then be made on the basis of the facts that Russia should retain
                    all such property, as provided in (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Fahy</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d399-a1.xml" xpointer="d399-a1"/>
            </div>
